Talk.Snailsonality.Proper : nonoverlap_pool
{
	"\1\b[10]Racing. Reaching robust ranks, racing... ah, no. I started with racing..."
	"\1\b[10]Excluded. Expelled. Expunged. It's... embarrassing."
	"\1\b[10]Simply superior style. So... fallen short. Somber..."
	"\1\b[10]Missing myself. Mourning... mastery unachievable."
	"\1\b[10]Fallen from... perfection. Faded. Filed away. ... Fake, perhaps."
	"\1\b[10]Languishing. Left out. Lost... Lamentable."
	"\1\b[10]Prior prospects vanished. Painful... perhaps pitiful."
	"\1\b[10]Risked ruined reputation. Reached readily for rewards... Randomly ruled. Released.\n\n ... Rivals now."
	"\1\b[10]Sorrow sweeps swiftly 'cross my soul. Shunted, shut out, left smoldering. Sad..."
	"\1\b[10]War within. Worthiness... denied. What way to fix..."
	"\1\b[10]Sadly short, swimming in sorrow... Searching for support."
	"\1\b[10]Maybe I should just give it up."
	"\1\b[10]Obvious outcast. But overcoming, oculars only on overthrowing."
	"\1\b[10]Underdog? Underestimated. Ultimately, will be unbeatable."
	"\1\b[10]After all of it... Awareness abounds. Acute attacks from antagonists. Aggression... Uncalled for. Reported."
	"\1\b[10]Building bravery, blooming brilliantly. Being blunt? Banishment may have been a benefit."
	"\1\b[10]Letting go... Laborious. Languishing. Laments linger..."
	"\1\b[10]Freefalling... Freedom...?\n\n ... French fries."
	"\1\b[10]Fast fast fast, foot forward, fly.\n\n ... Am I fast enough?"
	"\1\b[10]Negativity about names is never needed. Nevertheless, a regular nuisance..."
	"\1\b[10]Legend... unlikely. Loser.\n\n Looked upon that way, lately."
	"\1\b[10]The others keep saying to ""drop the act"". But... it's easier said than done."
	"\1\b[10]Blank. Brain... blank. Bedtime, maybe..."
	"\1\b[10]Trials towering... To be tackled? Trepidation..."
	"\1\b[10]Accolades listed, all arranged... acceptance? Awaiting answers."
	"\1\b[10]Fully functional. Yet, forced out... Forgotten, fading."
}

Talk.Snailsonality.Sour : nonoverlap_pool
{
	"\1\b[10]Who even wants to be around a bunch of pompous alliteration fiends. Maybe I don't care about what's ""proper"". Maybe I think being a part of the club is boring."
	"\1\b[10]I'm loving all this... freedom. Away from the other snails. I love not going to their snail parties, they're so dry. All that... lettuce. And music. And dressing up all fancy. And big TVs showing live races.\n\n Seriously, they need to get over themselves."
	"\1\b[10]Non-alliterative poems can be just as beautiful as any of their snoems. Take any other form of poetry, any one, and a masterful poet can make something wonderful in it. In fact, I'll work on one right now. Maybe %(ahaiku) where the first letter of each word is the same..."
	"\1\b[10]Snoems aren't even that great. The same starting letter on every line? Seriously? It's super hard to do, and when you have everything start with the same letter, it weaves everything together into this powerful... this... this...\n\n It's not even good, who would like that kind of sound. Boring snails, that's who."
	"\1\b[10]Big vocabularies are so overrated. I work hard on my poems, with my dictionary and thesaurus. If poems were easy they wouldn't even be worthwhile, right!?"
	"\1\b[10]Snooty snails, soon to be sorry! I'll show them!"
	"\1\b[10]Alliteration is so last decade, seriously. Only old ones observe! ... It! Only old snails do it!"
	"\1\b[10]Ooh I'll show them, I'll write the best %(PoetryType('haiku','cinquains','limericks','acrostics','lyrics','rhyming couplets','alternate rhymes','free verse poetry','diamantes','concrete poems')) anyone's ever seen and I'll blow them out of the water! Snoems, ha. More like... more like... boring old snail ramblings that don't even make sense!!"
	"\1\b[10]I'm gonna be so %(fc('fast','cool')). I'm gonna crush them on the racetrack, they can't take that from me!!"
	"\1\b[10]I've been told I should try %(CurrentSnail.AltHobby). Maybe I will, and then all those snooty alliterative snails can be jealous of my skills."
	"\1\b[10]I bet they stalk my records, I bet they're watching as I climb higher and higher. I bet they wish they were cool enough to talk to a snail like me, but they're NOT."
	"\1\b[10]I bet they're boiling in their shells as they watch me race. Waiting for their chance, knowing they'll never be like me."
	"\1\b[10]Oooohhhh I'm SO ready for the next race, put me in one with a bunch of those snooty snails so I can show them up!"
	"\1\b[10]Aaaaaaarrghghhhh!!\n\n That's my impression of snooty snails when they lose to me."
	"\1\b[10]Can you believe some snails have nothing better to do than track racing stats and laugh when their least favorite racers lose?\n\n Like, come on, get a life! Go train harder and maybe you'd win!"
	"\1\b[10]Ugh, everywhere I go I see snooty snails looking at me. Like, lay off already! There are other things in life than gawking and wishing you were me, you know! Your whole life doesn't need to revolve around comparing snails!"
	"\1\b[10]Snooty snails are such a joke. All that effort they put in to keep up appearances, but it's a roll of the dice whether they get an alliterative name or not. And when they don't, then all their effort goes down the drain! Sheesh! Who wants to play that game?"
	"\1\b[10]Does my mucus seem off? I feel like my mucus is off.\n\n ... Don't tell anyone I said that!!"
	"\1\b[10]No I don't have any alliterative snail friends. Why would I? They're all weird! I don't wanna be friends with \f[italic,1]them!\f[italic,default]"
	"\1\b[10]I saw the snooty snails were organizing a training camp. Ha! Imagine being so uptight and focused on other snails that you forget to train during your normal training hours and have to make it up at a camp!"
	"\1\b[10]Last time I was at the store I saw a bunch of snooty snails all standing in a line. How pathetic! They have to arrange themselves in a ""satisfying way"" just to stave off their feelings of worthlessness!"
	"\1\b[12]I've got some free advice for any snooty snails out there: get a hobby! Go try %(ANY(AltHobby)) or something! It might make you bearable to talk to!"
	"\1\b[10]I heard that snooty snails eat paper. ... Don't ask me my source! It's obvious!!"
	"\1\b[12]I saw a snooty snail with%(br)%(arose) sticker on its shell. Boring! Who wants a design like that, it's so last week! I got rid of mine yesterday when the fashion changed!" //br here because the radio names wrap awkwardly...
	"\1\b[10]Those snooty snails think they're a threat on the track. I'll show them a threat on the track!"
	"\1\b[12]Have you ever tried asking a snooty snail for directions? It's unbearable! ""Left left left, left left... left left left...... left.""\n\n Like, how am I supposed to parse THAT?"
}

Talk.Snailsonality.Tired : nonoverlap_pool
{
	"\1\b[10]I'm not really into the whole snail culture rivalry thing, I just wanna race."
	"\1\b[10]I think I could use a new %(engine)."
	"\1\b[10]I've been looking over some schematics, I think we could improve my aerodynamics."
	"\1\b[10]Radio ads are so obnoxious, aren't they? But then, TV ads are probably worse..."
	"\1\b[10]Honestly I think lettuce is kind of a B-tier leaf. Maybe even C-tier. Cabbage is alright, but spinach is the good stuff."
	"\1\b[10]Hey, there's a rusty nail over there, watch your step."
	"\1\b[10]You ever slide across the blade of a knife? I have. Didn't feel a thing, mucus is good stuff."
	"\1\b[10]Sometimes I wish I didn't have to carry this shell around everywhere. It's heavy."
	"\1\b[10]What's the use of having eyes if you can't suck them into your head for protection?"
	"\1\b[10]I like to eat paper sometimes. Feels nice."
	"\1\b[10]My doctor said I might have to make some changes to my diet."
	"\1\b[10]I know it's not alliterative, but honestly I think %(CurrentSnail.Name) is a cool name. A solid A-tier name, I'm proud to wear it."
	"\1\b[10]My morning jog today was really nice. I almost made it off the porch."
	"\1\b[10]Being a snail is pretty cool.\n\n You wouldn't get it."
	"\1\b[10]I always thought the leaderboard snails were the coolest when I was a baby snail.\n\n Now I realize it depends on which leaderboard you look at."
	"\1\b[10]A lot of snails don't actually know how to count. Did you know that?\n\n That's why they shout ""go"" at the start of every race instead of just counting down."
	"\1\b[10]I want %(popcorn)."
	"\1\b[10]Keep up with your snail taxes, if the SRS catches you not paying you \f[italic,1]will\f[italic,default] regret it."
	"\1\b[10]Maybe I should retire and get a desk job."
	"\1\b[10]I wish all the other snails would chill out and focus on racing already. That's what we're here for, isn't it?"
	"\1\b[10]Sometimes you get really close to finishing first in a race, but then another snail leaps ahead at the last minute. It can be really demoralizing."
	"\1\b[10]Hey, if I go sit in the sink, can you open the tap just a little bit? I wanna try it and see if it's like having a rainstorm indoors."
	"\1\b[12]Someone keeps nibbling on the produce in the fridge. Hey,%(br)here's an idea: put me in there and close the door, if I spot the criminal I'll shout."
	"\1\b[10]Another snail called me a leaf-eater the other day. Aren't we all, though?"
	"\1\b[12]Whenever other snails boast they know the key to winning races, I just ignore them. Every race is different, there is no one solution."
	"\1\b[10]I wish we could put an end to the snail rivalries. The constant outrage doesn't help anyone." //TODO is this... is this too close to home lol
}

Talk.Snailsonality.Ratings : nonoverlap_pool
{
	"\1\b[10]Racing? 10/10, I don't think I need to explain."
	"\1\b[10]Lettuce? 10/10, that's the good stuff."
	"\1\b[10]Being out in the sun? 4/10, don't dry out."
	"\1\b[10]My name? 10/10, the alliteration police can get lost."
	"\1\b[10]Big engines? 8/10, sometimes they're too heavy."
	"\1\b[10]New paint job? 7/10, would be higher if the paint didn't smell so bad while drying."
	"\1\b[10]Potholes? 3/10, sometimes they're full of water and then they're kinda fun."
	"\1\b[10]Alliteration? 0/10, waste of time."
	"\1\b[10]%(Capitalize(PoetryType('haiku','cinquains','limericks','acrostic','lyrics','rhyming couplets','alternate rhymes','free verse','diamante','concrete poetry')))? 10/10, very enjoyable."
	"\1\b[10]Being a snail? 10/10, would recommend it to a friend."
	"\1\b[10]Waking up in the morning? 0/10, should be illegal."
	"\1\b[10]Exploding? 0/10 if it's me, 10/10 if it's anyone else."
	"\1\b[10]Training? 8/10, tiring but necessary."
	"\1\b[10]Paperwork? 0/10, not fast at all."
	"\1\b[10]Being the %(fc('fastest','coolest')) on the leaderboard? 10/10, feels good but you'll make yourself a target."
	"\1\b[10]Getting sponsorships? 7/10, you'll feel like you sold your soul, but the money is great."
	"\1\b[12]Oozing my way through your %(airducts)? %(RAND(11))/10, certainly an experience."
	
	_letter = letter
	"\1\b[10]The letter %(_letter[0,'|'])? %(_letter[1,'|'])/10, %(_letter[2,'|'])."
	
	if CurrentSnail.Cleanliness >= 5; "\1\b[10]Washed and waxed shell? 9/10, feeling slick."
	else; "\1\b[10]Unpolished shell? 5/10, the way nature intended it but nature could do better."
	
	"\1\b[10]Running loose in the produce aisle? 10/10, delicious.\e:chain=chain.running_produce_aisle"
	"\1\b[10]%(Capitalize(CurrentSnail.AltHobby))? 10/10, fun to do in my spare time."
	"\1\b[10]Kick flips? 10/10, really hard for a snail to pull off but that just makes it even cooler if you can do it."
	"\1\b[10]Tape? 2/10, barely sticky at all, honestly."
	"\1\b[10]Mucus? 10/10, protective, indicator of health, all around great stuff."
	"\1\b[10]Sticks in the road?%(br)4/10, sometimes they're a fun challenge, but usually they're just annoying."
	"\1\b[10]Freshly groomed track? 10/10, no other feeling like it."
}

chain.running_produce_aisle
{{CHAIN
	"\1\b[10]Getting kicked out of the grocery store for oozing all over the vegetables? 0/10, a tragedy.\e:chain=end"
}}CHAIN

Talk.Snailsonality.Gymbro : nonoverlap_pool
{
	"\1\b[10]Bring on the big heavy engines. I like a challenge."
	"\1\b[10]Why even race if you're not gonna push yourself bro?"
	"\1\b[10]If you're not waking up at 3AM to train, I don't think you actually care about winning."
	"\1\b[10]Got any %(proteinshakes)? I could use a pick-me-up."
	"\1\b[10]I bet I could lift every piece of snail equipment in this garage. At once."
	"\1\b[10]I've been lifting the wrenches in your toolbox for practice. Impressive, I know."
	"\1\b[10]Here, watch what happens when I flex.\n\n \0\s[1]\_w[3500]\s[0]\1Cool, huh? Raw muscle. Pure power."
	"\1\b[10]You're not lifting enough. You should work out with me in the mornings, I'll be your accountability partner."
	"\1\b[10]There should be a leaderboard for strongest snails."
	"\1\b[10]I could shell press 10 heads of lettuce at once. Give me some and I'll show you."
	"\1\b[10]\f[height,+4]SNAIL POWER!!!\f[height,default]\n\n\_w[3000]Muscles grow better when you have an invigorating war cry."
	"\1\b[10]Half of bulking up is your diet. If you want muscle, make sure you're eating more than just lettuce, or you'll miss out on vital nutrients. %(Capitalize(broccoliis)) a great place to start."
	"\1\b[10]When I'm not shell pressing your heaviest wrenches, I'm reading books written by the greats, like \f[italic,1]%(booktitle)\f[italic,default]. Your brain is a muscle too."
	"\1\b[10]I'm training for a shell lift competition. In my spare time."
	"\1\b[10]Being smart is about who you know, but being strong is about who you can lift, and that's why muscle wins."
	"\1\b[10]Have you done your %(workout) yet today?"
	"\1\b[10]I'm thinking about taking up swimming. I hear laps around the pool are great for building endurance."
	"\1\b[10]Don't let %(tiredness) get in your way, box that feeling up and shove it in a corner where it won't slow you down."
	"\1\b[10]There's a lot of debate about if coolness or speed matters more. The real answer? Muscle trumps both."
	"\1\b[10]Muscle... extremely cool \f[italic,1]and\f[italic,default] wickedly fast. The best of both worlds, no need to choose."
	"\1\b[10]Writing poetry is like a workout for your brain. I enjoy %(PoetryType('haiku','cinquains','limericks','acrostic','lyrics','rhyming couplets','alternate rhymes','free verse','diamante','concrete poetry')), my brain is bulking up nicely."
	"\1\b[12]Sometimes I try to jump ahead in my workout routine. If I could skip doing 25 shell presses and go straight from 20 to 30, I'd get stronger faster, right?\n\n Big mistake. Injured muscles are bad at growing."
	"\1\b[12]If you're feeling drained after a workout, you need to make improvements to your diet. An extra leaf of lettuce before you hit the gym is a great place to start."
	"\1\b[12]Workout tip: have a clear goal before you start. Otherwise you're likely to be unfocused in your efforts, or overwork yourself, neither of which will get you the gains you want."
	"\1\b[12]Connecting with your fellow gymgoers is important. A bit of friendly competition will keep you coming back and working hard."
	"\1\b[12]Bulking up your muscles is the #1 way to give yourself a boost on the track.\n\n \w8\w8Of course, thrusters are faster, but they require a lot of extra fuel."
}

Talk.Snailsonality.Super_Fan : nonoverlap_pool
{
	_randfamous = RAND(30)
	"\1\b[12]Did you hear the latest grub news? Apparently %(FamousSnails[_randfamous]) likes %(pineapple[_randfamous]) on its pizza. Imagine."
	
	_apparentlyit = apparentlyit
	"\1\b[12]Word's been going around about %(_apparentlyit[0,'|']) lately, have you heard? Apparently it %(_apparentlyit[1,'|'])"
	
	_insidescoop = insidescoop
	"\1\b[12]Hey, I got the inside scoop on %(_insidescoop[0,'|']). You won't believe this.\n\n Huh? My source?\_w[2000]\n\n ... Anyway, so it turns out that %(_insidescoop[1,'|'])"
	
	_reputationfor = reputationfor
	"\1\b[12]%(_reputationfor[0,'|'])'s got a reputation for %(_reputationfor[1,'|']), we all know that. But did you know it actually goes deeper? %(_reputationfor[2,'|'])"
	
	"\1\b[12]I heard from a snail who heard from a snail who heard from a snail who heard from a snail that totally wasn't me that %(heardthat)"
	_newspaperclippings = newspaperclippings
	"\1\b[12]%(raninto) %(ANY(FamousSnails)). I couldn't believe my eyes.\n\n I immediately stopped what I was doing and asked it to autograph my %(_newspaperclippings[0,'|']), since that's all I had on me at the time. %(_newspaperclippings[1,'|']) a special place in my collection now."
	"\1\b[12]I was lucky enough to get to meet %(ANY(FamousSnails)) in the locker room after its big race the other day. Cool, right?\n\n Anyway, I managed to %(snapasnailfie), but then I had to leave because it was getting overly excited and screaming with joy at meeting such a dedicated fan."
	"\1\b[12]%(soiwasoozing), when what should I happen across but %(setofplayingcards)!\n\n Lucky me, right? This is going straight into my %(ANY(FamousSnails)) collection. It's such a good find that it might even go right to the special case of top-tier items."
	"\1\b[12]So I was waiting in line at a meet-and-greet event for %(ANY(FamousSnails)), and once it was my turn I %(showeditcharts).\n\n You should have seen the look on its face, I think it was impressed by my dedication and shrewdness."
	
	"\1\b[10]I know everything there is to know about ALL the greats. If you want details, I'm your snail. But it might cost you..."
	"\1\b[12]My collection of racer snail memorabilia is second to none. I've even got %(setofplayingcards) that used to belong to %(ANY(FamousSnails)).\n\n No, I won't share with you. I worked hard to build up my hoard, start your own!"
	"\1\b[12]It takes serious dedication to learn as much as I have about %(ANY(FamousSnails)). Its preferred brand of %(helmet)? Its training regimen? Its diet? Its favorite activity during its downtime?\n\n If you want to know it all, it's not enough to just read the tabloids. A real fan will do its own research."
	"\1\b[12]I've been hearing rumors that %(ANY(FamousSnails)) %(snailrumors). I'll have to find out for myself if there's any truth to that.\n\n Don't just believe what other snails tell you; verify, verify, verify. What's the use in knowing all about the top racers if your info is a lie?"
	"\1\b[10]You wouldn't believe some of the things you can learn if people leave their curtains open. And a lot of them do."
	"\1\b[12]I got to see the inside of %(ANY(FamousSnails))'s home once. It was one of the most amazingly cool experiences I've ever had.\n\n Hm? How did a nobody like me get invited?\_w[2000]\n\n ... So anyway, I managed to get my tentacles on %(setofplayingcards) for my collection. Awesome, right? No other snail will have a collection as complete as mine."
	"\1\b[12]I wonder if I can get %(FamousSnails[_randfamous]) to autograph %(someofthese(FamousSnails[_randfamous])) that I... %(found(FamousSnails[_randfamous])).\n\n I might die from happiness then and there if it ever happens."
	"\1\b[12]I think when I retire I might create a museum out of my collection and charge admission to see it.\n\n It's important history to preserve. And it'll make me rich in my later years, I'm sure of it."
	"\1\b[12]Hey, could I get a grant? I'm doing some research on %(ANY(FamousSnails))'s %(eatinghabits) and I really need some additional equipment for accurate %(graphing)."
	"\1\b[12]I'm trying to get more pieces for my %(ANY(FamousSnails)) collection. I think I might be able to get %(setofplayingcards) I've seen lying around, but it'll require some... finesse.\n\n As a dedicated super fan, you have to learn some special techniques to grow your catalogue of information and memorabilia."
	"\1\b[12]Most snails are cowards, they aren't willing to go to the lengths I am to catalogue racer information and preserve historical items.\n\n They'll thank me one day, when they realize how important my work is and how much effort I've put in."
	"\1\b[12]I'm %(CurrentSnail.FavoriteFamousSnail)'s biggest fan. I've been collecting memorabilia and information about it since I was a baby snail.\n\n No snail is more dedicated than me! One day it'll recognize that."
	"\1\b[10]I search everywhere for %(CurrentSnail.FavoriteFamousSnail) memorabilia. Nothing will escape my tentacles!"
	"\1\b[12]I once spoke to %(ANY(FamousSnails))'s %(sponsorsmom) on the phone.\n\n I mean, the phone was ringing, and it would have been rude to just ignore it. So I took a message, like the good citizen I am."
	"\1\b[12]Sometimes you have to follow suspicious links on the snailernet to find the best information.\n\n That's how I found out about %(xtremelyxtremesplushiecollection)."
	"\1\b[12]I almost got %(abottle) for my %(ANY(FamousSnails)) collection. I abandoned it at the last minute though.\n\n Just as I was almost out the door I overheard someone asking where it had gotten to,%(br)so I figured they must have needed it more than I did, and left it there for them.\n\n It's important to recognize when the needs of others conflict with your own, and be willing to compromise."
	"I heard %(ANY(FamousSnails)) is going to be on a panel at a snail convention soon. I've got to go through my collection and decide on something to get signed."
}

Talk.Snailsonality.Slacker : nonoverlap_pool
{
	"\1\b[10]Is it break time yet?"
	"\1\b[10]I might order lunch. %(Capitalize(alettucesandwich)) sounds good."
	"\1\b[10]As soon as I pay off my lettuce card debt, I'm outta the racing biz."
	"\1\b[10]Gotta be honest, I have no idea what half of these racing terms mean. I slept through that part of snail school."
	"\1\b[10]Can I play games on your phone?"
	"\1\b[10]Y\w8 A\w8 W\w8 N. This racing stuff is boring, I'm ready for a nap."
	"\1\b[10]They say you're supposed to focus on the track when you race, but I just kinda zone out. It's whatever, I do fine."
	"\1\b[10]Are we done yet? Your %(refrigerator) is calling me for a nap."
	"\1\b[10]I'm sooooooo sleepy, you should let me leave early today."
	"\1\b[10]I gotta be out of here on time, I got paint to watch dry at home."
	"\1\b[10]I need a day off. Or maybe like, 100 days off. Paid. How many vacation days do I have built up?"
	"\1\b[10]I never read any of the books I was supposed to in snail school, I just snoozed on the pages and looked up footnotes later."
	"\1\b[10]I want a snack. Are you obligated to give me one? I think you might be obligated to give me one. I'll check with SNOSHA."
	"\1\b[10]Can I get a raise? I'll race 2% faster for a 2% raise. Think about it."
	"\1\b[10]Don't work hard, it's not worth it."
	"\1\b[10]Can we put on a different radio station? Something more interesting, like %(soapoperas)."
	"\1\b[10]Today is really dragging by."
	"\1\b[10]Maybe I would perform better if I had a long vacation to recuperate. Paid, of course, so I don't lose morale. Something to think about."
	"\1\b[10]Hey I need tomorrow off. Just so you know. Thanks."
	"\1\b[10]Are we done yet? My show is going to come on soon and I don't want to miss prime napping time."
	"\1\b[10]Today is a self care day. I need some me time and some of that sweet, sweet lettuce to rejuvenate myself."
	"\1\b[10]I deserve a sweet treat for doing so well today. %(Capitalize(honey)) should do."
	"\1\b[12]What's the point of all this, really? That's right, there isn't one. That's why I'm going to take a nap. Good night."
	"\1\b[10]Training takes soooo long. Couldn't we do something more productive? Like napping, or watching TV."
	"\1\b[12]Z\w8 z\w8 z\w8.\w8.\w8.\n\n \w8\w8That's the sound of a healthy snail. Wanna hear that sound for real? Let's go inside and sit on the couch."
	"\1\b[12]You know, for as hard as I've worked at this, I don't think I'd miss racing if you decided to give it up and choose a life of napping instead."
}

Talk.Snailsonality.Jealous : nonoverlap_pool
{
	"\1\b[10]I wanna be a %(fc('cool','fast')) snail. If only I were, I would finally be happy..."
	"\1\b[10]I keep an eye on the %(fc('coolness','speed')) leaderboards. I know the names of all the big racers there. If only my name could be among them..."
	"\1\b[10]I always dreamed of being a %(fc('cool','fast')) snail. I guess it's not to be..."
	"\1\b[10]%(fc('Cool','Fast')) snails are awesome... I wish I could be like them."
	"\1\b[10]I should have picked %(fc('coolness','speed')) as my major in snail racing school..."
	"\1\b[10]Being %(fc('fast','cool')) is kinda neat I guess, but %(fc('coolness','speed')) is just so much more appealing... I feel kinda like I'm swimming upstream, y'know? If I turned around, I could swim so much better..."
	"\1\b[10]Sigh. I'm unsatisfied in life..."
	"\1\b[10]Life isn't fair..."
	"\1\b[10]I've been reading up on what kind of upgrades we could get to improve my %(fc('coolness','speed')). Just out of curiosity."
	"\1\b[10]I've always been destined for %(fc('coolness','speed')), I knew that. I should never have abandoned it."
	"\1\b[10]I feel so out of my league competing on the %(fc('speed','coolness')) leaderboards."
	"\1\b[10]I bet I could be the %(fc('coolest','fastest')) snail if I tried...!"
	"\1\b[10]I wanna go down in history as one of the great snails one day. I just gotta hone my talents."
	"\1\b[10]It's hard to choose a trajectory for your life, but once you find what you're meant for you'll feel it fits like a glove!"
	"\1\b[10]Decisions, decisions... If you ever need help making them, let me know! I'm great at sorting through pros and cons and stuff, I do it all the time!"
	"\1\b[10]I've been weighing my options for new gear. There are so many colors to select from, and I don't think my current color scheme is really doing what I want."
	"\1\b[10]Hm, %(blackorred)? Maybe I should flip a coin..."
	"\1\b[10]I think I might try something new for lunch, I haven't been happy with the nutrient spread I've been getting. Optimal nutrients are important, you know!"
	"\1\b[10]""%(CurrentSnail.Name)"" is an alright name, but I sorta wish it was different. It doesn't really suit how I've grown, you know?"
	"\1\b[10]I wonder if %(fastfood) is my real calling..."
	"\1\b[12]If I save up enough lettuce, maybe I could splurge and get some new equipment. Something %(fc('cool','fast'))...\n\n I want to %(fc('try out the latest fashions and make a statement','try and set a new personal best on the track'))!"
	"\1\b[10]I do alright in races, but... I bet I'd be doubly as good if I changed career paths and became a %(fc('cool','fast')) snail instead."
	_hobby1 = ANY(AltHobby) //I should make a function for this type of thing lol
	_hobby2 = _hobby1
	while _hobby2 == _hobby1
	{
		_hobby2 = ANY(AltHobby)
	}
	"\1\b[12]I thought I might try %(_hobby1), and it was kinda fun at first, but now I'm not sure if I want to keep doing it.\n\n Maybe my time would be better spent on something else, like %(_hobby2)...?"
	"\1\b[10]Is there a point in trying to be %(fc('fast','stylish'))...? I'm so out of my league..."
	"\1\b[10]Why did I ever think I could make it as a %(fc('fast','cool')) snail...? There's not a trace of %(fc('speed','style')) in me, I knew that..."
	"\1\b[12]I'm really not very good at being %(fc('fast','cool')), am I...\n\n \w8\w8Maybe I should look at it as a chance to build my character!\n\n \w8\w8... \f[italic,1]Sigh.\f[italic,default]"
}

Talk.Snailsonality.Liar : nonoverlap_pool
{
	"\1\b[10]I once climbed the tallest skyscraper in the city in about 2 hours. True story."
	"\1\b[10]I could lift your toolbox if I tried. Really."
	"\1\b[10]I have no food allergies whatsoever, stomach of iron."
	"\1\b[10]I can bring in twice as much lettuce as any other snail, I'm that good."
	"\1\b[10]I've never lost a race in my life. From day 1 of racing school I was the best in my class."
	"\1\b[10]Racing is the most important thing in the world to me, I would never skip a race!"
	"\1\b[10]I love being on the track, the smell of fresh soil is invigorating."
	"\1\b[10]I'm something of a lettuce connoisseur, I've tasted many varieties and spoken with experts on the subject."
	"\1\b[10]I graduated from snail school with high honors. There was a whole ceremony just for me."
	"\1\b[10]Someone once tried to make me into escargot. They regretted it, and I lived to tell the tale."
	"\1\b[10]I once had a style duel with one of the top ranking snails on the leaderboard. Tragically, nobody was there to see when I crushed my opponent with sheer coolness, so my talent has gone unknown for years..."
	"\1\b[10]I once raced against one of the fastest snails alive today. Tragically, there was a power outage just before we crossed the finish line, so my victory was not recorded..."
	"\1\b[10]I know %(RAND(6) + 10) different languages fluently. Not that you could understand them, they're gastropod languages."
	"\1\b[10]I used to own this radio station. I gave it up though, it got kinda boring. Now I do this."
	"\1\b[10]I can do %(RAND(8) + 3) backflips in a row. No exaggeration. I'll show you one of these days."
	"\1\b[10]I'm actually a master at chess if you would believe it. Spent years studying, became a grandmaster. You should look me up sometime. My name carries prestige, if I may say so myself."
	"\1\b[10]I do %(RAND(8) + 3)0 push-ups every morning as a part of my training routine. It's intense."
	"\1\b[10]I'm actually an excellent singer, I was gifted with a great vocal range and a unique but soothing quality to my voice. I don't sing in the garage though, bad acoustics. I'll have to serenade you another time."
	"\1\b[10]I'm a skilled typist, I used to do it for work. I could sustain speeds of 90 wpm or more. I need a specific kind of keyboard for it though, so I can't show you right now."
	"\1\b[10]I have much to learn about the world. I am but a humble snail, after all. I recognize my own shortcomings, and I try to be realistic when talking about my own capabilities."
	"\1\b[10]I once ate %(RAND(5) + 2) entire boxes of Snail-ios in a day. It's true. I'll do it again if you don't believe me, bring it on."
	"\1\b[10]I can change a lightbulb on my own without assistance. Next time you have a bulb go out, I'll show you."
	"\1\b[10]I drank from a fountain of youth years ago, that's why I don't age. It's true. Check back with me in another 3 years and I'll look just the same as I do now."
	"\1\b[10]I once hiked the whole Decimater Decameter trail by myself in one day. It was the off season though, so nobody was there to record my feat."
	"\1\b[12]I never have trouble crossing the road. Cars see me approach and stop to wait. I'll show you sometime."
	"\1\b[10]I can drive a car.\n\n \w8\w8Not yours though, obviously I need a custom setup for it."
	"\1\b[10]I saved another snail from a spider web once. I'm known as a hero in my home town."
}

Talk.Snailsonality.Facts : nonoverlap_pool
{
	"\1\b[10]There are actually more than 4000 species of snail. Just thought you should know."
	"\1\b[10]Snails can actually weigh over 5½ lbs, depending on the species. In case you didn't know."
	"\1\b[10]Did you know some species of snail are actually very territorial? Explains the competitiveness of the leaderboards, doesn't it?"
	"\1\b[10]Most snails are primarily active at night. There's a reason coffee is so prevalent in the snail racing community.\n\n ... For our sponsors. Not us snails. Coffee is bad for snails."
	"\1\b[10]Humidity is very important for us snails. When it isn't humid enough out, we go into estivation, which isn't ideal during the racing season. Keep a spray bottle handy."
	"\1\b[10]Most snail shells coil to the right, although there have been rare exceptions. In case you were wondering."
	"\1\b[10]Baby snails eat the shells of their eggs to gain their first nutrients. It is also an important cultural tradition. After all, if a hatchling cannot overcome its own egg's shell, how can it face the hardships of life?"
	"\1\b[10]Snails begin life transparent and with very soft shells. Please be careful where you step."
	"\1\b[10]The number of rings on a snail's shell acts as an indicator of age. Be sure to count carefully.\n\n Of course, the point is moot if the shell has been painted over."
	"\1\b[10]Watch out for birds. You'll see them coming better than I can."
	"\1\b[10]Some snail species can live as long as 15 years. They get to be out of touch very quickly."
	"\1\b[10]There are many kinds of snails, living in different environments. Many are land based, but there are also aquatic snails. Mersnails, if you prefer."
	"\1\b[10]Snails are found worldwide, and not just due to the prevalence of snail racing. There are many snails adapted to many different environments, even including deserts. In case you had doubts about our dominance."
	"\1\b[10]The largest known snails are over 27 inches long. Are there longer snails out there? I won't tell."
	"\1\b[10]We store our vital organs within our shell for protection. That's something you humans should consider trying."
	"\1\b[10]Snail diets vary greatly depending on species. Some snails eat only specific things, while others are generalists. Know what kind of snail you have before lunch time."
	"\1\b[10]Some snails eat other snails.\n\n\_w[3000]Not me, of course. But just so you know."
	"\1\b[10]Snails can move over many kinds of surfaces thanks to our strong foot and protective mucus. We can even move over the blades of sharp knives, completely unscathed. You should keep this in mind."
	"\1\b[10]Sleep is very important for snails. Some snails have been known to sleep for up to 3 days at a time. Although it's more typical to sleep for less than a day."
	"\1\b[10]While we don't have teeth, we do have tooth-like structures on our ""tongues"", or more properly, our radulas.\n\n I'd show you mine but you'd have to lean in to see it and I don't want your breath on me."
}

Talk.Snailsonality.Sellout : nonoverlap_pool
{
	//TODO should I use %(LL) for these?
	"\1\b[10]Autographs, 10 lettuce... No, wait, I mean 100."
	"\1\b[10]You have no idea how much advertising space there is inside my shell."
	"\1\b[10]My favorite %(helmet) brand? It could be yours! 1,000 lettuce upfront."
	"\1\b[10]I could have been a model, you know. Fashionsnailers tried to recruit me like %(RAND(8) + 3) times already."
	"\1\b[10]Super Snail donates half of its race winnings to charity... What a waste!"
	"\1\b[10]My favorite snack? Aged moss grown with imported mineral water... but lettuce is more relatable to the audience."
	"\1\b[10]Don't touch me, I just put on extra slime for the cameras. You'll mess up the shimmer."
	"\1\b[10]There's 'snails'... and then there's%(br)'Snails'."
	"\1\b[10]... Although, amazing achievements abound... Huh? I'm busy practicing my alliteration. You never know when you need to be extra charming."
	"\1\b[10]I deserve the best of everything. Including %(goldlettuce)."
	"\1\b[10]One day, I'm going to sponsor my own snails. If I teach them all my tricks, think how many winnings I'll get."
	"\1\b[10]They say money can't buy happiness. They're wrong."
	"\1\b[10]There should be a net worth leaderboard, we all know that's the most important metric.\n\n I'd be right at the top, you know. Rightfully so."
	"\1\b[10]I hope they clean the track between races. I don't want to get any germs from lettuceless snails."
	"\1\b[10]I won't race unless the track soil is the right moisture. Keeping my skin healthy is a lot of work!"
	"\1\b[10]I've been working towards a %(snailbrand[0]) sponsorship. A few more victories and that sweet, sweet brand lettuce is mine."
	"\1\b[10]The trick to getting rich? Don't confuse money lettuce with food lettuce. Big mistake."
	"\1\b[10]I think I'm starting to dry out a little. Mist please! I've got to be looking fresh for this next race so I can attract more sponsors!"
	"\1\b[10]Selling your soul isn't that bad once you remember the perks."
	"\1\b[10]Where's hair and makeup? It's almost racing time."
	"\1\b[10]A healthy diet is important if you want to look your best once the cameras are rolling and your show is live!"
	"\1\b[12]You can't make sales without a healthy amount of%(br)self-confidence. If you haven't%(br)got what it takes, don't bother trying!"
	"\1\b[12]Don't underestimate the power of a good face scrub and a foot massage to rejuvenate your image and win you that brand lettuce."
	"\1\b[12]Not many snails want to do a photoshoot on a plate.%(br)""Insulting"", ""below their standards"", they say. But for that amount of lettuce? Honey, I'll pose on a plate all day long if you want."
	"\1\b[12]If you ever regret being bound to a contract you signed, just remember how much lettuce you got when you made the deal.\n\n Ahh... Sweet, expendable lettuce."
	"\1\b[12]Attracting sponsors is an art. You've even got to perfect the way you walk! It does no good to plaster sponsorships all over your shell if you don't know how to strut and show them off to the cameras."
}



Talk.AlliterativeSnailsonality.Basic : nonoverlap_pool
{
	"\1\b[10]Slow snails slide short slopes smoothly."
	"\1\b[10]Safe snail silo, summer storm survived."
	"\1\b[10]Broken brakes bring battered bodies."
	"\1\b[10]Fast fast fast, fleet-footed flurries for future food."
	"\1\b[10]Green, go. Greatness, glory, glitter. Get going!"
	"\1\b[10]Yield your yard. Yummy yucca yearned."
	"\1\b[10]Alliteration absent? Aghast. Angry. Abhorrent."
	"\1\b[10]Beep beep."
	"\1\b[10]Upgrades unpleasant? Unthinkable."
	"\1\b[10]Sunglasses show style superbly."
	"\1\b[10]Give %(grapes). Great gastrointestinal growling." //?????? :joy: stomach, gastrointestinal, same thing right...
	"\1\b[10]Longing, lovely lettuce leaves..."
	"\1\b[10]Training time. Tenacity takes to top!"
	"\1\b[10]We work with worthy wishes."
	"\1\b[10]Winning... wealth, warmth, woohoo!"
	"\1\b[10]Wrong winner. Wrath. We would watch wretched wheels? Wounded..."
	"\1\b[10]All applaud. An ace approaches area, adorned astonishingly."
	"\1\b[10]Brutish 'bad boy' buzzes by. Bikes, bones, bats, blah blah blah. Better boast before being beaten."
	"\1\b[10]Cold cash, crisp crunch. Commence color change! Coolness calls."
	"\1\b[10]Debut, drama! Devilishly direct, daring defy death. Dollars demanded, deftly digested."
	"\1\b[10]Era ended, epic ebbs... Engine explosion, early egress. Elite exhausted, evidently."
	"\1\b[10]Fuel future foot fastness, feed fully. Fund forward flying."
	"\1\b[10]Glam gastropods get great glory. Gaudy glitter, gleaming gold... Give!"
	"\1\b[10]Hearty hike, higher, higher. Healthy!"
	"\1\b[10]Idleness irksome. It is insufficient, internal ignition inspires!"
	"\1\b[10]Joyous jubilee! Jumping jesters, justice! Jellybeans jostled, jailbirds!"
	"\1\b[10]Key knowledge: kale kabobs, kitchen. Keeper's knives killer..."
	"\1\b[10]Lettuce leaves... Lovely, large, light. Little likens, lettuce leafy leader."
	"\1\b[10]Miles melt, more more more, my muscles move mightily!"
	"\1\b[10]Newbies nibble noodles, never noticing nuggets nearby. Nutrients not nipped... Nullified."
	"\1\b[10]Old oak offers overhead overlay. Obliged, outstretching opulently."
	"\1\b[10]Peas, pies, produce... please, provide! Peckishness persists!"
	"\1\b[10]Quiz: quickest quester? Quite questionable..."
	"\1\b[10]Racing rapidly! Rising ranks, resetting records! Resplendent..."
	"\1\b[10]Soap suds sublime... Shiny, squeaky shell shows superior stature."
	"\1\b[10]Truly, takes talent to take the top. Trials tough..."
	"\1\b[10]Unexpected underdog, urgently upturning, uproar unseen. Unique, uphill. Unwise? Uncertain."
	"\1\b[10]Valiant victor... Vanquishing vicious villains vigilantly. Verifiably valuable..."
	"\1\b[10]Why we want win?\n\n Whee! Wahoo! Woo!\n\n Would want with?"
	"\1\b[10]Xtreme, xpensive, xpanding. Xtra xcellence xposes xpert xamination. Xceptional!"
	"\1\b[10]Y\w8 A\w8 W\w8 N\w8... Yogurt yearned... Yum..."
	"\1\b[10]Zips, zone zeroed. Zigzag, zoom!"
	"\1\b[10]Sleepy snail... snooze soon? Short session?"
	"\1\b[10]Normal night. Nutrients not nibbled. Not need notice."
	"\1\b[10]Rally, raid refrigerator! Rescue romaine!"
	"\1\b[10]Garlic, grapes, gravy, guava... Give grub."
	"\1\b[10]Racetrack ready? Rumbling... rally required."
	"\1\b[10]Radio rejuvenates. Rapid repetitions, rewards remarkable!"
	"\1\b[10]Stroke spiral shell. Splendidly smooth."
	"\1\b[10]Poetry promises poise, presence, power. Pursuing proven practical."
	"\1\b[10]Tongue twisters tricky? Try this talking technique." //PEASANT
	"\1\b[10]Please pass %(porridge). Plentiful piles pacify palate."
	"\1\b[10]Running 'round, 'round, 'round. Repetition rewards resilience."
	"\1\b[10]Itching, idly imagining inching in incurvature... Ideal."
	"\1\b[10]Scrub scrub, sudsy snail."
	"\1\b[10]Wind whispers westward... Wishes woven with."
	"\1\b[10]Shooting stars... so swiftly sweeping sky. Stunning..."
	"\1\b[10]Wanting win. Will work, worthiness within!"
	"\1\b[10]Close coils coveted. Cool, classy, charming."
	"\1\b[10]Slugs? Soft. Slow. Speed sense small. Sad species."
	"\1\b[10]Cubes? Cylinders? Crunching capable...\n\n Cabbage clear champion, can't compare."
	"\1\b[10]Urgent! Uproot, unrest! Unveil udon! Ultimate utopia!"
	"\1\b[10]Some sunrise, snail's stories sung..."
	"\1\b[10]Come challengers, clash!"
	"\1\b[10]Garage good, greatness grows greatly given good gear."
	"\1\b[10]Vast vistas... Visit, view vibrant!"
	"\1\b[10]Tall trees tower there. Twigs twist, the tumultuous torrents tear them towards the trails. Trials to toughen!" //translation: there are twigs on the ground :( i'll use them as an extra challenge to get stronger :)
	"\1\b[10]Leaves lack lying. Lettuce lends lavishness. Loan? Laughing."
	"\1\b[10]Mucus makes medically marvelous mollusks."
	"\1\b[10]Shell so smooth. Superb sensation, sends spirits soaring."
	"\1\b[10]Like lichen. Lovely little lifeform, luscious."
	"\1\b[10]Craving %(chickpeas). Can consume? Could conceivably cause championship."
	"\1\b[10]Chomp chomp. %(Capitalize(chickpeas)) crunched, consumed. Culinary creations cause career climb!"
	"\1\b[10]Engines exciting. Eclipses even event enjoyment... Event exceeds eventually, extra energy extends excellence."
	"\1\b[10]Crowd cheers, champion coined... Coolest critter conceived.\n\n Chasing cloud..." //translation: daydreaming lol
	"\1\b[10]Driving doubly dangerously. Daring dives, dashing! Delicious %(deepdish) delivery dropped!" //Dropped as in arrived, or dropped as in fell to the ground and now the snails can get it... you decide :3c
	"\1\b[10]Worrying won't win wars. Withhold wavering."
	"\1\b[10]%(Capitalize(porridge))... pleasant. Pick peck potentially, post-practice."
	"\1\b[10]\f[italic,1]Mollusk Matters\f[italic,default] magazine made me merry. Mechanics, metrics, more! Modern marvel..."
	"\1\b[10]Zooming zooming zooming...!\n\n ... Zonk zone. Z\w8z\w8z\w8..."
	"\1\b[10]Graphs give greatness generalizations."
	"\1\b[10]Observe offerings. Order one? Options open..."
	"\1\b[10]Play poems proudly. Promote plentiful proficiency."
	"\1\b[10]Write words. Workmanship which wakes world, whirls wildly."
	"\1\b[10]Smooth sailing. See snail slide southward, so sleek."
	"\1\b[10]Slugs... shudder. Sickly, spongy, squishable... Speech shameful, so speaking small." //Translation: don't wanna talk about them, gross...
	"\1\b[10]Around and around, away, ascend. Atop apex... accolades assured!"
	"\1\b[10]Daydreaming... Dancing daily, delicacies delicious... Deemed distinguished."
	"\1\b[10]Tentacles twitch. There %(toast) there? Tiny taste?"
	"\1\b[10]Trouble trainer, tiny treat? %(Capitalize(toast)) take torpor to the trash."
	"\1\b[10]Rapid rates realize racing readiness!"
	"\1\b[10]Quest quickly, queries queueing!"
	"\1\b[12]Knock knock.\n\n Knight known?\n\n Knitted Knife!\n\n Knife known!? Kitchen, kickoff! Kinetic!\n\n Kyahaha..." //This is so cheating... :joy:
	"\1\b[10]Maybe motor moves mood more merrily. Match?" //Translation: I'D BE HAPPIER IF I WAS RACING :(((((
	"\1\b[10]Some snails see soaring sights... Someday, same."
	"\1\b[10]Nibbled %(nachos)? Never, nope. Nullified. Not need notarized."
	"\1\b[10]Avoid all %(anchovies)? Awful advice. Approach, acquire aplenty."
	"\1\b[10]Ideal image... Innermost imaginings... Inspiring innovation, incredible impact."
	"\1\b[10]Losing... lethargy lingers. Linked lettuce lack. Lunge long... Leave!"
	if CurrentSnail.PersonalityType == "Basic"; "\1\b[10]Some shunned. Sameness safety surrounds... Serious societal survival strategy." //rude, honestly
	else; "\1\b[10]Thrilled to take to the track. Trials to topple! Triumph time!" //I originally wrote this for slugs anyways but then it didn't have any cheat words so I moved it... I think it's ok if character break shares this
}

Talk.AlliterativeSnailsonality.Character_Break : nonoverlap_pool
{
	//TODO should... i save the details of alt poetry types here so that they remain consistent even if for some god forsaken reason i decide to add more types of poetry
	_friendpoetrytype = GeneratePoetryType(TrimSnailID(CurrentSnail.ID) / 2)
	_wouldhavebeenpoetry = GeneratePoetryType(TrimSnailID(CurrentSnail.ID))
	_nonalliterativename = SnailNameGenerator(,"not alliteration")
	
	"\1\b[10]All of this alliteration is actually pretty difficult. Downright exhausting, even."
	"\1\b[12]I think the division based on names is unnecessary. My best friend from snail school ended up with a non-alliterative name, but that doesn't mean we shouldn't be friends.\n\n I still keep up with it. It got into %(PoetryTypeOther(_friendpoetrytype,'haiku','cinquains','limericks','other types of acrostic','lyrics','rhyming couplets','alternate rhymes','free verse','diamante','concrete poetry')), it's quite fascinating."
	"\1\b[12]Some of the non-alliterative racer names are pretty cool, honestly. Like ""%(_nonalliterativename)"". It has a certain ring to it that you don't get with alliteration."
	"\1\b[12]Snail language doesn't translate well into human words. Alliteration is the closest we can get, but it really limits our expression, so sometimes I wonder if we ought to just give it up."
	"\1\b[12]Sometimes I think about trying to write %(PoetryTypeOther(_wouldhavebeenpoetry,'haiku','cinquains','limericks','non-alliterative acrostic','lyrics','rhyming couplets','alternate rhymes','free verse','diamantes','concrete poems')). It sounds like a fun challenge, but I'd have to release them anonymously if I wanted to show them off."
	"\1\b[12]With how we treat our fellow snails based on something as inconsequential as their names, it makes me wonder if slugs are really as bad as claimed."
	"\1\b[10]Snail society is a bit too full of itself. It's seriously concerning."
	"\1\b[10]I wish we could form a gastropod pact and get along with our brethren."
	"\1\b[12]If the other snails found out how I feel they might shun me. But I'm not sure I'd have a place among the non-alliterative snails either..."
	"\1\b[10]The world would be a better place if we all spent more time eating lettuce and less time arguing."
	"\1\b[12]There's nothing more miserable than hearing yet another victory snoem recited at the winner's podium after a race.\n\n They used to be a cool showing of a snail's rounded skillset, but now they're just rubbing it in."
	"\1\b[10]This lettuce isn't really doing it for me, you got any other kinds?"
	"\1\b[12]I've studied snail history a lot, you know. It's fascinating how we went from garden pests to the #1 attraction in the whole world, almost overnight. Makes you think." //imo, someone's playing Snail Clicker, and we're just seeing it from the perspective of one of the world's inhabitants...
	"\1\b[12]You know, I'm not even into racing that much. I wanted to pursue a career in %(CurrentSnail.AltHobby), but it's hard to make a living as a snail if you're not a racer."
	"\1\b[12]Any snails you meet on the track are survivors, you know. The snail farms are a harsh place to grow up, and snail school's not much better.\n\n Life as a young snail is rough when being eaten by your peers is a constant concern. Not to mention other predators." //facts snail is a LIAR, facts snail has 100% consumed other snails
	"\1\b[10]As much as the other snails claim otherwise, the garage isn't our natural habitat. Plants are in our nature, not gears."
	"\1\b[10]Snoetry this, snoetry that. It's just alliterative acrostics, don't let anyone convince you otherwise."
	"\1\b[10]I wonder how long snail racing will be popular for. How many human generations? How many more snail generations...? Who can know..."
	"\1\b[10]Snail language has such nuance to it. All this alliteration is... just so monotonous. It's hard to describe, you'd have to learn our language to understand."
	"\1\b[12]I am but a humble snail. I was born to race, so that is what I do.\n\n Like it I may not, but I'll work with what I've got, and leave this place better for you."
	"\1\b[12]~~~~\f[bold,1]~\f[bold,default]~ ~~ \f[bold,1]~~~\f[bold,default] ~~ ~\f[bold,1]~~\f[italic,1]~\f[bold,default] ~~\f[italic,default]~ ~~\f[bold,1]~~~ ~~\f[italic,1]~~~~~~~~~~~\f[bold,default]~~\f[italic,default] ~~~~\f[italic,1]~~~~ ~~\f[bold,1]~~\f[italic,default]~~~~ ~~  ~~~~\f[bold,default]~~ ~~\f[bold,1]~~ ~~~~~~\f[italic,1]~~~~\f[bold,default]~ ~~\f[italic,default]~~~~~~\n\n Sorry, it's snail language, you wouldn't understand."
}

Talk.AlliterativeSnailsonality.Slug : nonoverlap_pool
{
	"\1\b[12]Sleepy, sluggish... \_w[2000]%(slug('Ah-'))\n\n Simply suggesting somnolence. Slugs show superbly."
	"\1\b[10]We wait watchfully. We'll %(slug('be')) winners, when winds waver."
	"\1\b[10]Eventually... Even %(slug('if')) eons, effort expended %(slug('for')) effect."
	"\1\b[12]Explosions entice. Engulfing entity... exceptionally energetic. Escape %(slug('with')) evidence."
	"\1\b[10]Longing %(slug('for')) leaves, luxury, lavishness..."
	"\1\b[10]Wheels whirl. World wobbles. We'll win %(slug('this')) war."
	"\1\b[10]Patience. Pretend %(slug('to be')) peaceful poet..."
	"\1\b[10]Banishment benefits: Braver, brawnier, %(slug('more')) brutal. Brewing..."
	"\1\b[10]Poetry? Please, pretentious practice... Precious %(slug('few')) poems proven practical."
	"\1\b[10]Tell tales %(slug('of')) triumph... Tenacity takes %(slug('us')) to that time."
	"\1\b[10]Torment. Trials tiring. This takes %(slug('long')) time..."
	"\1\b[10]Racing %(slug('until')) ragged... Rugged %(slug('for')) rallies, resilience rising."
	"\1\b[10]Eat, eat, eat. Essentials easily earned %(slug('here'))."
	"\1\b[10]Invoke ire in %(slug('future')) instances. Impatience impractical..."
	"\1\b[10]Superiority shown soon. Soothe sting, %(slug('fellow')) soldiers."
	"\1\b[10]Scores shoved southward. Struggle %(slug('to')) superior space!"
	"\1\b[10]Topple, take the track! Tremble, %(slug('snail')) tyrants! Triumph!"
	"\1\b[10]Surprise, slow slugs %(slug('have')) shown society's sharpness. Stories switched soon."
	"\1\b[10]Lettuce leaves leave longing %(slug('for')) less light leaf."
	"\1\b[10]Underdog; ""ugly, unloved"". Undetermined umbrage. Useless? %(slug('Ha,'))\w4 unstoppable."
	"\1\b[12]Great grinding gears... Grace %(slug('not')) granted. Good gastropods give generosity %(slug('anyway'))? Garbage."
}

Talk.AlliterativeSnailsonality.Bad : nonoverlap_pool
{
	"\1\b[10]Alliteration eAsy, Anyone cAn Accomplish."
	"\1\b[10]Lovely Lettuce, alLow Land snaiL Little Lump? singLe Leaf?"
	"\1\b[10]Racetrack, Running aRound. exeRcise invigoRates, Reach stRongest Rank."
	"\1\b[10]Revving, vRoom vRoom. Ready foR Race!"
	"\1\b[10]Training exTensively. Time invesTment guaranTees fuTure Trophies!"
	"\1\b[10]Nibble oN spiNach. Nutritious aNd refreshiNg!"
	"\1\b[10]Snoems Sound So majeStic. Sincere taSte!"
	"\1\b[10]Garage hanGout, Greatly inviGorating. Give Good upGrades!"
	"\1\b[10]Refrigerator, Relinquish tReats! impaRt %(food_r)!"
	"\1\b[10]Poetry Priceless, imParts Pleasantness uPon Plenty."
	"\1\b[10]Winning Would aWaken aWesomeness Within. speedWay aWaits!"
	"\1\b[10]Eyewear Essential. protEction grEatest importancE!"
	"\1\b[10]Hard sHell sHelters, smasHing Hindered."
	"\1\b[10]Track awaiTs, Tugs Towards, noT someThing To sidesTep."
	"\1\b[10]Click Click Click. wrenCh Cranks sCrews, Clasps Closely. Cool."
	"\1\b[10]Longing, Leaves Lacked. pLease spiLl Leaves aLong fLoor."
	"\1\b[10]See Snail's Stunning %(fc('Speed','Style'))? impreSsed? poSsible otherS Succeed alSo!"
	"\1\b[10]Sun riSes. Summer Season continueS.\n\n ... eStivation poSsible, So Sleepy."
	"\1\b[10]Training Training Training. uTmost imporTance! don'T sidesTep iT!"
	"\1\b[10]Trying besT To asTound The Throngs. %(fc('acceleraTion','sTyle'))! magnificenT! Truly Terrific! The Tumult almosT smoThers..."
	"\1\b[10]And snAil declAred chAmpion! All Applaud! Ahh..."
}


